$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Representative procedure for the microwave
assisted Cu/C-catalyzed Ullmann aryl ether coupling; compound 2, Scheme
2. Cu/C (30 mg, 0.05 mmol, 1.8 mmol/g), 1,10-phenanthroline (90 mg, 0.50
mmol), cesium carbonate (390 mg, 1.2 mmol), and estrone (271 mg, 1.0
mmol) were added to a oven-dried Biotage® 2-5 mL process vial under argon
at rt. Dry dioxane (2.0 mL) was added by syringe and the slurry allowed
to stir at rt for 30 min. 3-Bromopyridine (0.145 mL, 1.5 mmol) was added
via micro-syringe and the resulting heterogeneous mixture was heated in
the microwave with the following settings; Temperature: 220 °C, Time:
1800 sec., Fixed hold time: On, Sample Absorption: Normal, Pre-stirring:
10 sec. After cooling to rt, the crude reaction mixture was filtered
through Celite® and the filter cake was further rinsed with ethyl
acetate. Volatiles were removed on a rotary evaporator and the crude
product was then purified by flash chromatography on silica gel, (3/2
Hexanes/Ethyl Acetate) Rf = 0.25, to yield 299 mg (86%) as a colorless
solid. (Table 2, entry 4). Colorless oil. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.70
(dd, J = 1.2, 7.6 Hz, 1H), 7.44 (dt, J = 1.2, 7.2 Hz 1H), 7.39 (m, 2H),
7.15 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 6.99 (m, 2H), 6.95 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H), 1.344
(s, 9H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 154.1, 147.3, 133.4, 127.3, 127.3,
127.0, 122.5, 119.3, 118.9, 34.6, 31.7. IR (neat NaCl plate): 3042, 2965,
2870, 1609, 1491, 1322, 1248, 1137, 759 cm-1. MS (EI): m/z (%): 294(23),
279(100), 251(5), 199(5), 125(5), 118 (5), 57(5). HREIMS calcd. for
C17H17F3O [M+] = 294.1231, found 294.1243.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Ullmann reaction, second stage microwave irradiation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Copper-in-Charcoal (Cu/C) Promoted Diaryl Ether Formation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Lipshutz, Bruce H.; Unger, John B.; Taft, Benjamin R.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2007), 9(6), 1089-1092

