$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4-(2-Methoxynaphthalen-1-yloxy)-naphthalene-1-carbaldehyde (19). To a
solution of 2-methoxy-1-naphthol 4 (18, 191 mg, 1.10 mmol) and
4-fluoro-1-naphthalenecarbaldehyde (8, 174 mg, 1.00 mmol) in CH3CN (3 mL)
was added at room temperature 2-tert-butyl-1,1,3,3,-tetramethylguanidine
(0.24 mL, 1.20 mmol). The reaction mixture was heated at 70 °C for 1 h,
cooled to room temperature, poured into 1.0 M HCl (10 mL), and extracted
with CH2Cl2 (2 × 20 mL). The combined organic layer was washed with H2O
(10 mL), dried (MgSO4), and concentrated under reduced pressure.
Chromatography on SiO2 (hexanes/EtOAc, 7:3) afforded 260 mg (79%) of 19
as a white solid. mp 112-113 ° C (hexanes/EtOAc); IR (neat) 2841, 2726,
1682, 1570, 1510, 1377, 1276, 1218 cm-1; 1H NMR δ 10.18 (s, 1H), 9.41
(dd, 1H, J= 8.4, 1.2 Hz), 8.78 (dt, 1H, J= 8.4, 0.8 Hz), 7.91-7.78 (m,
4H), 7.76-7.70 (m, 1H), 7.71 (d, 1H, J= 8.1 Hz), 7.46-7.39 (m, 3H), 6.48
(d, 1H, J= 8.1 Hz), 3.89 (s, 3H); 13C NMR δ 192.5, 160.0, 148.7, 139.4,
135.9, 132.5, 130.0, 129.9, 128.6, 128.2, 127.4, 127.2, 127.0, 126.0,
125.3, 124.8, 122.8, 120.9, 115.0, 106.4, 57.1; MS (EI) m/z (rel
intensity) 328 (M+, 100), 285 (23), 268 (37), 257 (17), 239 (27), 228
(22), 173 (17), 127 (37); HRMS (EI) calcd for C22H16O3 328.1099, found
328.1092.
