$DATUM N-[4-(2-methoxyphenoxy)phenyl]-pyridin-3-ylmethylamine A solution of
(4-Bromophenyl)-pyridin-3-ylmethylamine (5.00 g, 19.0 mmoles) in pyridine
(20 mL) was treated with guaiacol (6.27 mL, 57.0 mmoles) and anhydrous
K2CO3 (3.94 g, 28.5 mmoles). The reaction was warmed to 90°C and then
treated with cupric oxide (1.81 g, 22.8 mmoles). The resulting mixture
was refluxed for 44 h, cooled to room temperature and diluted with ethyl
acetate. After washing with 6 portions of 10% aqueous ethylenediamine
(until the aqueous phase is no longer purple), 0.1 M K2CO3, and then
brine, the organic layer was dried over Na2SO4, filtered, and
concentrated. The residue was chromatographed on silica gel eluting with
70:30 to 60:40 CH2Cl2/ethyl acetate to yield 4.6 g (79%) of the title
compound. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) 8.64 (1H, bs), 8.53 (1H, m), 7.70 (1H,
m), 7.23-7.29 (1H, m), 6.95-7.04 (2H, m), 6.79-6.89 (4H, m), 6.60 (2H,
m), 4.33 (2H, s), 3.88 (3H, s). MS found 307.0 [M+H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of Allosteric Potentiators for the Metabotropic Glutamate 2
Receptor: Synthesis and Subtype Selectivity of
N-(4-(2-Methoxyphenoxy)phenyl)-N-(2,2,2-
trifluoroethylsulfonyl)pyrid-3-ylmethylamine
