$DATUM 1,4-Bis(4-nitrophenoxy)-2-phenylbenzene (BNPPB) was synthesized by a
nucleophilic substitution reaction of pchloronitrobenzene with
2-phenylhydroquinone. In a threeneck flask equipped with a nitrogen
inlet, a condenser and a magnetic stirring bar, p-chloronitrobenzene
(11.7 g, 74 mmol) was dissolved in 40 mL of DMF. 2-Phenylhydroquinone
(5.0 g, 27 mmol) was added and themixture was stirred until dissolving,
and potassium carbonate (8.5 g, 61 mmol) was added. The reaction mixture
was heated with stirring at 140°C for 24 h under nitrogen atmosphere and
then poured into 200 mL of water. A yellowish solid precipitated out of
the solution overnight. After filtration, the residual reactants and
potassium carbonate were eliminated from the solid by washing with water
and ethanol. The product was collected and dried in vacuum at 90°C for 8
h. The crude dinitro-aromatic compound BNPPB was purified by
recrystallization from glacial acetic acid. A 78% yield of a yellow
powder. Mp 143-147°C; 1H-NMR δ (ppm): 8.30-8.28 (d, 2H, Ar), 8.18-8.15
(d, 2H, Ar), 7.50-7.48 (d, 2H, Ar), 7.40-7.32 (m, 6H, Ar), 7.30-7.28 (d,
2H, Ar), 7.09-7.07 (d, 2H, Ar); FTIR (KBr): ν (cm-1) = 1341 (NO2), 1236
(-O-ether).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
