$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-iodo-2-(2-nitrophenoxy)benzene. A mixture of 2-iodophenol (3.30 g, 15.0
mmol, 1.00 equiv.), 2-fluoronitrobenzene (2.12 g, 15.0 mmol, 1.00
equiv.), and K2CO3 (4.15 g, 30.0 mmol, 2.00 equiv.) was stirred in DMSO
(30.0 mL) at 100 °C overnight. The reaction mixture was quenched with
water and extracted with EtOAc. The combined organic layers were washed
with water, dried over MgSO4 and the volatiles were evaporated. Column
chromatography (5% EtOAc in pentanes) yielded 4.01 g of 36 (78%).
1-iodo-2-(2-nitrophenoxy)benzene, yield 4.01 g (78%). 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 8.00 (dd, J = 8.0 & 1.6 Hz, 1H), 7.89 (dd, J = 8.0 & 1.6 Hz,
1H), 7.52-7.47 (m, 1H), 7.38-7.33 (m, 1H), 7.24-7.19 (m, 1H), 7.00-6.94
(m, 2H), 6.86 (dd, J = 8.4 & 1.2 Hz, 1H). Spectra were identical to that
previously reported.7
