$DATUM 7-Nitrodibenzo[b,d]furan-3-ol (2). Compound 14 (500 mg, 2.01 mmol) and
Cs2CO3 (1.96 g, 6.02 mmol) were dissolved in MeCN (10 mL) and stirred for
30 min at 150 °C under MW irradiation conditions. EtOAc (30 mL) was added
to the mixture and the organic layer was washed with H2O (2 × 20 mL),
dried over MgSO4, filtered and concentrated in vacuo to afford the crude
product as a brown solid. Recrystallization from MeCN furnished the title
compound. Yield: (360 mg, 78%), pale brown needle-shaped crystals. Mp
248-249 °C; Rf = 0.19 (EtOAc-heptane, 1:2). IR (ATR): 3427, 2923, 1614,
1560, 1507, 1457, 1320, 1279, 1206, 1130, 1050, 903, 841, 805, 769, 754,
728 cm-1. 1H NMR (600 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ = 10.44 (s, 1 H), 8.50 (d, J = 2.0
Hz, 1 H), 8.26 (dd, J = 8.5, 2.0 Hz, 1 H), 8.21 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 1 H),
8.08 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 1 H), 7.11 (d, J = 2.1 Hz, 1 H), 6.96 (dd, J = 8.5,
2.1 Hz, 1 H). 13C NMR (151 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ = 160.1, 159.5, 154.1, 144.7,
130.5, 123.2, 119.9, 118.8, 113.6, 113.3, 107.2, 98.1. GC-MS: tR = 5.451
min, m/z = 229 [M+]. UV/Vis (MeOH): λmax = 356 nm (ε = 20 × 103
M-1·cm-1). Anal Calcd for C12H7NO4: C, 62.89; H, 3.08; N, 6.11. Found: C,
62.90; H, 3.15; N, 6.09.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation
