$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of Potassium
2,5-bis(4-nitro-2-trifluoromethylphenoxy)benzenesulfonate (BNFPBS). Into
a 500 mL three-necked flask equipped with a mechanical stirrer, a
nitrogen inlet and outlet and a Dean-Stark trap with a condenser, 45.11 g
(200.5 mmol) of 1-chloro-4-nitro-2-(trifluoromethyl) benzene, 22.93 g
(100 mmol) of potassium 2,5- dihydroxybenzenesulfonate and 13.8 g (100
mmol) of K2CO3 were placed. DMF (180 mL) and toluene (35 mL) were added
as solvent and azeotropic reagent, respectively. The mixture was refluxed
at 130 °C for 3 h. After fully dehydration, toluene and remain water were
removed and the mixture were stirred at 150 °C for another 4 h. The
solution was cooled to 80 °C after the reaction was complete and poured
into ethanol. crude product was filtered and dried. After
recrystallization from a mixture of deionized water and ethanol, pure
product was obtained. Synthesis of Potassium
2,5-bis(4-nitrophenoxy)benzenebenzenesulfonate (BNPBS). Synthesis of
BNPBS was accomplished using a similar procedure of synthesis of BNFPBS,
and 1- chloro-4-nitrobenzene was used to replace 1-chloro-4-nitro- 2-
trifluoromethylbenzene. Yield, 78%. FTIR: 1045, 1085 (-SO3). 1H NMR
(DMSO-d6, ppm): 7.72 (d, J=8.0Hz, 4H); 7.20 (s, 1H); 6.8 (d, J=6.0Hz,
1H); 6.78 (d, J=8.0Hz, 1H); 6.67 (d, J=8.0Hz, 4H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM toluene used for azeotropic removal of water
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
