$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for
La0.9Ce0.1Co0.6Cu0.4O3-Catalyzed Ullmann Couplings of Phenols
La0.9Ce0.1Co0.6Cu0.4O3 (4.4 mg, 5 mol%) was added to a mixture of aryl
halide (0.71 mmol), phenol (1.00 mmol), Cs2CO3 (325 mg, 1.00 mmol) and 1
drop of EtOAc in toluene (1 mL) in a microwave vial. The tube was flushed
with argon, sealed and heated in an oil bath at 110 °C for 48 h. The
reaction mixture was filtered through a Chem Elut CE1005 drying column,
eluting with Et2O (3 × 10 mL). Combined filtrates were concentrated in
vacuo and purified by column chromatography to afford the desired
product. Yield 78%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Copper- and palladium-containing perovskites: Catalysts for the Ullmann
and Sonogashira reactions
