$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Preparation of Substituted
3-Amino-4-(2-iodophenoxy)phenyl sulfones 11. A suspension of substituted
2-iodophenol (20 mmol), 4-fluoro-3-nitrophenyl sulfone (10 mmol), and
potassium carbonate (40 mmol) in dimethylsulfoxide (30 mL) was heated at
55 °C for 8 h. After cooling to room temperature, the reaction mixture
was diluted with water (50 mL) and extracted with ethyl acetate (3 × 150
mL). The combined organic phase was washed with water (3 × 100 mL) and
dried over anhydrous magnesium sulfate. The solvent was removed under
reduced pressure to give crude nitro halide used in the next step without
further purification. The solution of crude nitro halide and tin(ΙΙ)
chloride dihydrate (100 mmol) in ethyl acetate (100 mL) was stirred at
room temperature for 18 h. The reaction mixture was quenched with aqueous
sodium hydroxide, and the aqueous phase was extracted with ethyl acetate
(3 × 100 mL). The combined organic phase was washed with water (3 × 100
mL) and dried over anhydrous magnesium sulfate. The solvent was
evaporated in vacuo, and the residue was purified by flash chromatography
on silica gel with a mixture of hexane and ethyl acetate as eluant to
afford the corresponding product. 3-Amino-4-(2-iodophenoxy)phenyl sulfone
(11a). 78% yield; mp 216−217 °C; 1H NMR (300MHz, CD3SOCD3) δ 7.91 (dd, J
= 1.2, 8.1 Hz, 2H), 7.41−7.30 (m, 4H), 7.01−6.96 (m, 6H), 6.55 (d, J =
8.3 Hz, 2H), 5.62 (s, 4H); 13C NMR (300MHz, CD3SOCD3) δ 155.66, 147.31,
140.78, 140.56, 137.37, 131.14, 127.41, 121.20, 117.18, 115.89, 113.77,
90.92; MS (EI) m/z 684 [M+]; HRMS Calcd. for C24H18I2N2O4S 683.9077,
found 683.9048.
