$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3,3'-Di-tert-butyl-5,5'-bis(2-chloro-4-nitrophenoxy)biphenyl-2,2'-diol
(17): A mixture of 16 (0.600g, 1.82 mmol), 3-chloro-4-fluoro-nitrobenzene
(0.639g, 3.64 mmol) and K2CO3 (0.753g, 5.45 mmol) in acetonitrile (60 mL)
was heated slowly to reflux. After heating overnight, the reaction was
cooled down, poured into water and extracted with EtOAc. The combined
organic layers were dried over MgSO4 and removed under reduced pressure.
After purification using column chromatography (5/5: CH2Cl2/C7H16), 17
was obtained. Light yellow solid, yield (0.91 g, 78%). 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400
MHz) δ 8.38 (d, 2H, J=3 Hz), δ 8.07 (dd, 2H, J1=9 Hz, J2=3 Hz), δ 7.16
(d, 2H, J=3 Hz), δ 6.90 (m, 4H), δ 5.31 (s, 2H, OH), δ 1.45 (s, 18H, tBu)
ppm; 13C NMR (CDCl3, 75 MHz) δ 159.5, δ 149.7, δ 147.6, δ 142.5, δ 140.7,
δ 126.7, δ 124.2, δ 123.8, δ 123.7, δ 120.9, δ 120.2, δ 115.8, δ 35.6, δ
29.5 ppm; mp 129-132 °C; HRMS calcd for [C32H30Cl2N2O8] 640.1379, found
640.1397.
