$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 7-Bromo-3-fluoro-2-methoxy-9H-xanthen-9-one (5d). Step 1. To a slurry of
4-bromophenol (115 g, 663 mmol), 2-bromo-4-fluoro-5-methoxybenzoic acid
(150 g, 602 mmol), cesium carbonate (393 g, 1205 mmol) in toluene (600
mL) were added copper (I) trifluoromethanesulfonate toluene complex (4.67
g, 9.03 mmol) and ethyl acetate (2.95 mL, 30.1 mmol). Reaction was
stirred at 110°C for 16 hours. Reaction was cooled to rt and poured into
a separatory funnel containing 1 L of water and 1 L of ethyl acetate. The
aqueous layer was washed with ethyl acetate (2 x 500 mL). The organic
layer was washed with brine and concentrated to provide 245 g of a green
solid. This solid was taken up in 1 L of ethyl acetate and 1 L of 3 N
HCl. The layers were separated and the aqueous layer was extracted with
ethyl acetate 2 x 500 mL. The combined organics were washed with brine,
dried over sodium sulfate and concentrated. 212.5 g of a yellow solid
which was used without purification in the next step. Step 2. A 3-L three
neck flask equipped with an overheard stirrer was charged with sulfuric
acid (803 mL, 1510 mmol) and heated to 60°C. To this was added crude
solid from the previous portion-wise over 15 minutes. The resulting dark
brown slurry was maintained at 60°C for 1 hour. The mixture was removed
from the oil bath and slowly added to a 5 L flask containing 1 L of
ice-water mixture. After the addition was complete another 2 L of ice
water was added and the resulting slurry was stirred vigorously with an
overhead stirrer for 3 hours. The thick mixture was filtered, and the
derived white solid was washed well with water (5 x 1 L), followed by 3 N
NaOH (3 x 500 mL) and finally water (2 x 500 mL). The solid was dried
under a stream of air and the resulting chunky light yellow solid was
ground into a fine powder and dried in vacuo at 50°C for 2 hours.
7-bromo-3-fluoro-2-methoxy-9H-xanthen-9-one (152 g 78 % yield). 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3) δ ppm 8.47 (d, J=2.4 Hz, 1 H), 7.78 - 7.84 (m, 2 H),
7.40 (d, J=8.9 Hz, 1 H), 7.25(d, J=8.9 Hz, 1 H) 4.03 (s, 3 H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
