$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: l-3. Typical procedure for direct “one-pot”
synthesis of dibenzo[b,f] oxepine lactam A nitrogen-flushed microwave
vial was equipped with a magnetic stirring bar and charged with 4 Å
molecular sieves (200 mg). The vial was flame dried for 10 min under high
vacuum and purged with N2. After cooling to room temperature,
isoindolinone (0.3 mmol), 2-bromobenzaldehyde (0.6 mmol), CuBr (10 mol
%), and Cs2CO3 (0.9 mmol) were added sequentially. The reaction mixture
was suspended in pyridine (5 mL). Then, the reaction vial was sealed and
placed into a heating block at 150 °C for 24 h. The mixture was cooled to
room temperature, filtered through a Celite pad, and washed with acetone.
The resulting solution was concentrated with a rotary evaporator, and the
residue was purified by silica gel flash column chromatography
(EtOAc/hexanes). Dibenzoxepine lactam.
1-Methylbenzo[6,7]oxepino[4,3,2-cd]isoindol-2(1H)-one (10a).
8-Fluoro-5-methoxy-1-methylbenzo[6,7]oxepino[4,3,2-cd]isoindol-2(1H)-one
(10l) Yield 78%, yellow solid. mp 198.9 °C; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ
7.34 (d, 1H, J = 8.2 Hz), 6.95-6.89 (m, 2H), 6.78-6.67 (m, 2H), 5.70 (s,
1H), 3.92 (s, 3H), 3.23 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (75.5 MHz, CDCl3) δ 166.2, 163.5
(J = 249.6 Hz), 154.7 (J = 11.0 Hz), 152.0, 141.3, 136.9 (J = 2.5 Hz),
132.3 (J = 9.2 Hz), 127.2, 124.0 (J = 4.0 Hz), 122.1, 119.0, 115.1, 112.0
(J = 21.1 Hz), 110.4 (J = 24.8 Hz) 107.0, 56.8, 25.8; HRMS (EI) calcd for
C17H12FNO3 [M+] 297.0801, found 297.0803.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM thermal, one-pot etherification/Aldol condensation cascade reaction,
molecular sieves used, sealed tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Dibenzoxepine Lactams via a Cu-Catalyzed One-Pot
Etherification/Aldol Condensation Cascade Reaction: Application toward
the Total Synthesis of Aristoyagonine
