$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for preparing
2-aminodiphenyl ethers 4l, 4m, and 4q The 2-aminodiphenyl ethers 4l,12
4m, and 4q were prepared from stirring the mixture of the substituted
fluorobenzene and 2-aminophenol with potassium carbonate in 10 mL of DMSO
overnight. To the mixture 50 mL of water was added and then 30 mL of
ethyl acetate was added. The organic layer was washed with water (50 mL x
3), and the products were obtained by removal of the EtOAc. The crude
product was purified by flash chromatography using silica gel (EtOAc:hex
1:4). 2-(4-Nitrophenoxy)aniline (4l):12 4-Fluoro-1-nitrobenzene (212 μL,
2.0 mmol), 2-aminophenol (0.22 g, 2.0 mmol), and potassium carbonate (1.2
g, 9.0 mmol) were used. 5-(2-Aminophenoxy)-2-nitrobenzonitrile (4q):
5-Fluoro-2-nitrobenzonitrile (0.33 g, 2.0 mmol), 2-aminophenol (0.22 g,
2.0 mmol), and potassium carbonate (1.2 g, 9.0 mmol) were used. The
product was a brown solid (0.40 g, 78%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.29
(d, J = 9.2 Hz, 1H), 7.34 (d, J = 2.7 Hz, 1H), 7.25 (dd, J1 = 9.2 Hz, J2
= 2.7 Hz, 1H), 7.17-7.12 (m, 1H), 6.94 (dd, J1 = 8.0 Hz, J2 = 1.2 Hz,
1H), 6.89 (dd, J1 = 8.0 Hz, J2 = 1.2 Hz, 1H), 6.84-6.79 (m, 1H), 3.73
(br, 2H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 162.2, 142.5, 139.9, 138.7, 128.0,
127.6, 122.2, 121.4, 120.1, 119.5, 117.4, 114.7, 110.1. HRMS (EI) Calcd
for C13H9N3O3: 255.0644; found: 255.0645.
