$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 4-(diethylamino)-2-(3-(diethylamino)phenoxy)benzaldehyde
(NA570). Compound 9 (1 g, 6.05 mmol), 10 (1 g, 3.9 mmol) and Na2CO3 (620
mg, 6.05 mmol) were heated to 140oC in 40 mL of DMF with constant
stirring for 6 hrs. Then the mixture was cooled to room temperature
before filtering off the solid. DMF was then removed under reduced
pressure to give a viscous residue, which was purified by a flash column
using a mixture of petroleum ether and EtOAc (20:1, v/v) as eluent. NA570
(1.04g, colourless solid) in a 78% yield. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3 ): δ
10.15 (s, 1H), 7.80 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.13 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 6.44
(d, J = 8.0 Hz 1H), 6.42 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 6.40 (d, 1H), 6.25(dd, J =
8.0 Hz 1H), 6.07 (d,J = 2.4Hz,1H), 3.32 (m, 8H),1.14 (m, 12H); 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3 ): δ187.0, 162.2, 158.3, 153.6, 149.5, 130.2, 129.9,
115.9, 107.3, 106.8, 105.2,102.4 99.9, 44.8, 44.4,12.6, 12.5; EI-HRMS
(m/z): [M+H]+ calcd. for C21H28N2O2 ,340.2151; found 340.2153.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Williamson ether synthesis
