$DATUM 4-(2-Iodophenoxy)-2-nitrobenzaldehyde (6). 4-Fluoro-2-nitrobenzaldehyde
(5) (500 mg, 2.95 mmol), 2-iodophenol (650 mg, 2.95 mmol), CuBr (425 mg,
2.95 mmol), and K2CO3 (815 mg, 5.9 mmol) were dissolved in dry pyridine
(10 mL) and heated to 60 °C for 12 h. The reaction was subsequently
cooled to r.t., filtered, taken into Et2O (100 mL) and washed with 1 M
NaOH (2 x 100 mL), water (2 x 100 mL), and brine (100 mL). The organic
layer was dried over Na2SO4 and the volatiles were evaporated. The
residue was purified by silica gel chromatography (hexanes:EtOAc, 92:8),
affording 4-(2-iodophenoxy)-2-nitrobenzaldehyde (6) as a white solid in
77% yield (840 mg, 2.27 mmol). 4-(2-Iodophenoxy)-2-nitrobenzaldehyde,
yield 77% yield (840 mg, 2.27 mmol). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ =
7.04-7.14 (m, 2 H), 7.18-7.26 (m, 1 H), 7.42-7.50 (m, 2 H), 7.92-7.99 (m,
2 H), 10.31 (s, 1 H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 90.1, 112.4, 121.3,
133.2, 125.3, 128.3, 130.7, 131.9, 140.9, 151.7, 153.8, 161.7, 186.9.
HRMS: m/z calcd for C13H8NO4I [M+Na]+: 391.9390; found: 392.0123.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
