$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure 2 for the coupling of an
aryl bromide and a phenol catalyzed by CuO: To a solution of aryl bromide
derivative (100 mM in anhydrous pyridine) in a Schlenk tube were added a
phenol derivative (2 equivalents) and K2CO3 (2.5 equivalents). CuO (0.1
equivalent) was then added and the mixture was heated at 130 °C with
stirring for 48 hours. After cooling to room temperature, the copper
salts were removed by filtration. The filtrate was diluted with Et2O and
washed successively with HCl 1M, saturated aqueous NaHCO3 and brine. The
organic phase was dried over MgSO4 and the solvents were evaporated. The
residue was purified by flash chromatography on silica gel
(cyclohexane/EtOAc : 8/2). Compound 30: Using General procedure 2,
compound 30 was synthesized from 28 and compound 298 and obtained.
Compound 36: Using General procedure 2, compound 36 was synthesized from
35 and 298 and obtained. White solid (104 mg, 77%). 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ = 8.05 (dd, J=1.9, 7.8, 1H), 8.02 (dd, J=1.9, 7.8, 1H), 7.43
-7.39 (m, 2H), 7.35 -7.25 (m, 4H), 7.25 -7.18 (m, 3H), 7.16 (dt, J=2.3,
5.8, 2H), 6.92 (dd, J=1.5, 8.0, 1H), 6.87 (td, J=1.5, 7.5, 1H), 6.75
(ddd, J=1.5, 7.5, 8.0, 1H), 6.46 (dd, J=1.5, 8.0, 1H), 5.15 (s, 2H), 5.12
(s, 2H), 3.64 ppm (s, 3H); 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ = 165.8, 165.3,
153.9, 149.5, 147.9, 137.6 (2xC), 135.7, 135.6, 128.6 (4xC), 128.3 (2xC),
128.2, 127.9, 127.5 (2xC), 127.1, 126.8, 124.8, 122.5, 121.5, 115.8,
115.1, 71.4, 67.4, 52.5 ppm; LC-MS (C4, ESI-MS) rt = 8.79 min, m/z = 469
[M+ H]+, 486 [M+NH4]+ 491 [M+Na]+ ; HRMS (ESI) m/z calculated for
C29H25O6 469.1646, found 469.1642 [M+ H]+.
