$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the reaction of 4-n-alkylphenoxides with
1,2,3,4-tetrafluorobenzene. 60% (w/w) sodium hydride in mineral oil (1.1
equiv.) was charged to a microwave vial (10-20 ml, Biotage) equipped with
a magnetic follower and sealed. The microwave vial was evacuated under
high vacuum and back-filled with argon three times to create an inert
atmosphere. The sodium hydride was washed with dry hexane (10 ml), which
was removed using a syringe, and replaced with dry THF (10 ml). The
4-n-alkylphenol (1.0 equiv.) was dissolved in dry THF (5 ml), under an
atmosphere of argon, and carefully added to the sodium hydride mixture,
with stirring, to produce sodium 4-n-alkylphenoxide and hydrogen gas.
When the evolution of hydrogen gas had stopped 1,2,3,4-tetrafluorobenzene
(1.0 equiv.) was added to the microwave vial and the reaction was heated
to 180 °C for 1 hr, left to cool, poured on to water (30 ml) and
extracted with dichloromethane (3 × 30 ml). The combined extracts were
washed with water (50 ml) and dried (MgSO4). The mixture was filtered and
the solvent removed in vacuo and purified by column chromatography on
silica gel. 2-(4-Ethylphenoxy)-1,3,4-trifluorobenzene (14) Reaction of
60% (w/w) sodium hydride in mineral oil (0.360 g, 9.01 mmol),
4-ethylphenol (1.000 g, 8.19 mmol) and 1,2,3,4-tetrafluorobenzene (0.887
g, 5.91 mmol). 2-(4-Ethylphenoxy)-1,3,4-trifluorobenzene 14 (1.102 g, 74
%) as a colourless oil. (Found: C, 66.74; H, 4.39. C14H11F3O requires C,
66.66; H, 4.40 %); 1H NMR (700 MHz; CDCl3): δ 1.22 (3H, t, 3 J HH 7.7, CH
3), 2.61 (2H, q, 3 J HH 7.7, CH 2), 6.82 (2H, dm, 3 J HH 8.7, 2'-H), 6.93
(1H, dddd, 3 J HH 9.4, 3 J HF 9.3, 4 J HF 4.4, 5JHF 2.4, 6-H), 6.99 (1H,
dddd, 3 J HH 9.4, 3 J HF 9.4, 4 J HF 4.6, 4 J HF 8.0, 5-H), 7.13 (2H, dm,
3 J HH 8.7, 3'- H); 13C NMR (176 MHz; CDCl3): δ 15.63 (s, CH3), 28.01 (s,
CH2), 110.72 (ddd, 2 J CF 21.0, 3 J CF 7.7, 4 J CF 4.1, 6-C), 111.96 (dd,
2 J CF 19.4, 3 J CF 8.5, 5-C), 115.21 (s, 2'-C), 128.90 (s, 3'-C), 133.21
(m, 2-C), 139.17 (s, 4'-C), 145.13 (dddd, 1 J CF 254, 2 J CF 14.8, 3/ 4J
CF 4.6, Ar-C), 147.80 (dddd, 1 J CF 246, 2 J CF 10.9, 3/ 4 J CF 3.6,
Ar-C), 152.19 (ddd, 1 J CF 248, 3 J CF 2.8, 4 J CF 2.8, 1-C), 155.52 (s,
1'-C); 19F NMR (658 MHz; CDCl3; CFCl3): δ -131.05 (1F, dddd, 3 J FH 9.3,
J FH 4.6, 4 J FF 2.3, 5 J FF 13.6, 1-CF), - 140.04 (1F, dddd, 3 J FF
20.4, 3 J FH 9.4, J FH 4.4, 5 J FF 13.6, 4-CF), -148.23 (1F, dddd, 3 J FF
