$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM methyl 4-(2-cyanophenoxy)-1-naphthoate (31-2). To a solution of
methy4-fluoro-1-naphthoate (0.32g, 1.6 mmol) and 2-hydroxy benzonitrile
(0.24 g, 2.0 mmol) in dimethyl sulfoxide (10 mL) was added potassium
carbonate (0.55 g, 4.0 mmol). The reaction mixture was stirred at 130 °C
for 12 hours. The reaction was cooled to ambient temperature, then poured
into water (100 mL) and extracted with ethylacetate (100 mL). The organic
layer was washed with water (80 mL), dried over sodium sulfate,
concentrated and purified by column chromatography (silica gel: ethyl
acetate: petroleum ether = 1: 8)to providemethyl
4-(2-cyanophenoxy)-1-naphthoate. Colorless oil, yield 0.36 g, 77%.
