$DATUM 4-(4-Methoxynaphthalen-1-yloxy)-naphthalene-1-carbaldehyde (17). To a
solution of 4-methoxy-1-naphthol (16, 191 mg, 1.10 mmol) and
4-fluoro-1-naphthalenecarbaldehyde (8, 174 mg, 1.00 mmol) in CH3CN (3 mL)
was added at room temperature 2-tert-butyl-1,1,3,3,-tetramethylguanidine
(0.24 mL, 1.2 mmol). The reaction mixture was heated at 70 °C for 1 h,
cooled to room temperature, poured into 1.0 M HCl (10 mL), and extracted
with CH2Cl2 (2 × 20 mL). The combined organic layer was washed with H2O
(10 mL), dried (MgSO4), and concentrated under reduced pressure.
Trituration of the residue with cold hexanes/EtOAc (4:1) afforded 251 mg
(77%) of 17 as a light brown solid. mp 174-175 °C (hexanes/EtOAc); IR
(neat) 2841, 2729, 1683, 1570, 1509, 1460, 1385, 1234 cm-1; 1H NMR δ
10.18 (s, 1H), 9.40 (dd, 1H, J= 8.5, 0.6 Hz), 8.71 (d, 1H, J= 8.5 Hz),
8.35 (dd, 1H, J= 8.4, 0.6 Hz), 7.84-7.78 (m, 2H), 7.73-7.69 (m, 1H), 7.70
(d, 1H, J= 8.0 Hz), 7.54-7.51 (m, 1H), 7.46-7.41 (m, 1H), 7.22 (d, 1H, J=
8.3 Hz), 6.83 (d, 1H, J= 8.3 Hz), 6.59 (d, 1H, J= 8.0 Hz), 4.06 (s, 3H);
13C NMR δ 192.4, 161.2, 153.6, 143.7, 139.2, 132.5, 130.1, 127.9, 127.4,
127.1, 127.0, 126.4, 126.0, 125.5, 125.3, 122.8, 122.6, 121.6, 117.6,
107.5, 103.4, 56.0; MS (EI) m/z (rel intensity) 328 (M+, 100), 313 (20),
268 (6), 239 (8), 174 (19), 127 (32); HRMS (EI) calcd for C22H16O3
328.1099, found 328.1099.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Highly Oxygenated Dinaphthyl Ethers via SNAr Reactions
Promoted by Barton's Base
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
