$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for preparing 2-aminodiphenyl ethers 4l, 4m, and 4q The
2-aminodiphenyl ethers 4l,12 4m, and 4q were prepared from stirring the
mixture of the substituted fluorobenzene and 2-aminophenol with potassium
carbonate in 10 mL of DMSO overnight. To the mixture 50 mL of water was
added and then 30 mL of ethyl acetate was added. The organic layer was
washed with water (50 mL x 3), and the products were obtained by removal
of the EtOAc. The crude product was purified by flash chromatography
using silica gel (EtOAc:hex 1:4). 2-(4-Nitrophenoxy)aniline (4l):12
4-Fluoro-1-nitrobenzene (212 μL, 2.0 mmol), 2-aminophenol (0.22 g, 2.0
mmol), and potassium carbonate (1.2 g, 9.0 mmol) were used. The product
was a brown solid (0.36 g, 77%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO) δ 8.22 (d, J =
9.2 Hz, 2H), 7.04-7.00 (m, 3H), 6.92 (dd, J1 = 8.0 Hz, J2 = 1.4 Hz, 1H),
6.85 (dd, J1 = 8.0 Hz, J2 = 1.5 Hz, 1H), 6.63-6.58 (m, 1H), 5.05 (br,
2H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Additivity of Substituent Effects in Aromatic Stacking Interactions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
