$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4-(4-Fluorophenoxy)perfluoro[2.2]paracyclophane (1c). To a mixture of
4-fluorophenol (28 mg, 0.25 mmol) in anhydrous THF (10 mL) was added 60%
sodium hydride (11 mg, 0.275 mmol). The resulting reaction mixture was
stirred for 30 min, after which F8 (124 mg, 0.25 mmol) was added. The
mixture was stirred at rt overnight, and then it was concentrated to
dryness. The residue was purified by column chromatography (hexanes) to
obtain 1c (110 mg, 76.9%) as a white solid: mp 98-99 ºC; 1H NMR δ 7.01
(m, 2H), 6.81 (m, 2H); 19F NMR δ -99.46 (ddd, J 1=249.0 Hz, J 2=29.1 Hz,
J 3=10.4 Hz, 1F), -100.4 (ddd, J 1= 253 Hz, J 2=31 Hz, J 3=10 Hz, 1F),
-100.6 (ddd, J 1=251 Hz, J 2 =29 Hz, J 3=10 Hz, 1F), -101.0 (d, J=251 Hz,
1F), -104.5 (dd, J 1=245 Hz, J 2=62 Hz, 1F), -104.9 (ddt, J 1=249 Hz, J 2
=73 Hz, J 3=15 Hz, 1F), -105.4 (ddt, J 1=251 Hz, J 2=62 Hz, J 3=14 Hz,
2F),-119.0 (m, 1F),-122.0 (m, 1F),-131.7 (m, 2F) ,-132.3 (dd, J 1=56 Hz,
J 2=10 Hz, 1F), -133.2 (dt, J 1=64 Hz, J 2=17 Hz, 1F),-134.6 (m,
1F),-135.3 (m, 1F). Anal. Calcd for C22H4F16O: C 44.92, H 0.69. Found: C
45.24, H 0.72.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Reactions of Nucleophiles with Perfluoro[2.2]paracyclophane
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
