$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Attachment of Amines
to Merrifield resin: The amine (2.5 mmol) is placed in a round bottom
flask and stirred in 150 ml of tetrahydrofuran for 15 min at room
temperature. The bortrifluoro etherate (0.037 mol) is added and the
mixture is stirred for 15 min. at room temperatur e and then cooled down
to -15 °C. The isoamylnitrite (3.5 mmol) is added and the mixture is
stirred at this temperature for two hours. In a three necked round bottom
flask with a overhead stirrer the resin (5 g [1.0 mmol/g]) is swollen in
100 ml of diethylether and 13.5 ml of pyridine and cooled down to -25 °C.
Than the diazonium-salt is added with 100 ml of acetonitrile and the
mixture is slowly warmed up to room temperature. General Procedure for
the Ullmann -Nicolaou Reaction: The triazene resin (0.5 g [0.9 mmol/g]),
copper bromide dimethylsulfide complex (2.5 mmol) and potassium carbonate
(3 mmol) are given into a vial. 10 ml of acetonitrile, 5 ml of pyridine
and the phenol (2.5 mmol) were added under argon. The vial is closed and
shaked for two days at 75 °C. The mixture is cooled to room temperature
and than washed first with water and than alternately with a solution
(5%) of sodium diethylaminodithio carbamate (Cupral) in DMF and methanol,
until the washing solution became colorless. Then, the general washing
protocol was continued. In case of bisbrominated resin 3 {4}, the amount
of the copper complex, the base and the phenol were doubled. General
Cleavage Protocol to the Azides: The triazene resin 500 mg [0.9 mmol/g]
is swollen in 10 ml of dichloromethane and mixed with 0.2 ml of
azidotrimethylsilane and 0.15 ml of trifluoro acetic acid. The mixture is
shaked for 30 min. Then, the mixture is filtered and the solution
evaporated under reduced pressure. 1-Azido-2-(2´-methoxy)phenoxy-benzene
6{1,2}: 77%. - 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 3.84 (s, 3 H, OCH3),
6.75-7.10 (aromatic area, 8 H). - 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 56.2 (+,
OCH3), 113.2 (+, C-3), 118.6 (+, C-6), 120.2 (+, C-3´), 120.8 (+, C-4´),
121.2 (+, C-5), 123.9 (+, C-5´), 125.0 (+, C-4), 125.6 (+, C-6´), 130.4
(q, C-1), 145.2 (q, C-2), 149.6 (q, C-1´), 151.1 (q, C-2´). - IR
(CH2Cl2): ν = 2113 (N3), 1606 (arene), 1501 (diaryl ether) 1115 (OMe)
cm-1. - MS (EI), m/z (%) = 241 (M+, 15), 212 (5), 198 (30), 184 (55), 182
(100), 170 (45), 154 (10), 142 (10), 128 (10), 115 (10), 90 (20), 78
(25), 63 (15), 51 (15). - HRMS: calcd 241.0851, found 241.0861
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM combinatorial, solid-supported reaction, fourth stage attachment to
Merrifield resin, Ullman-Nicolaou reaction fifth stage
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Efficient Synthesis of Highly Substituted Diaryl Ethers on Solid Supports
Using the Ullmann Reaction
