$DATUM Synthesis of 3-nitro-4-(p-tolyloxy)benzaldehyde 36: A solution of
p-cresol (1 g, 5.4 mmol) and 4-chloro-3-nitrobenzaldehyde (0.58 g, 5.4
mmol) in 0.63 N aqueous NaOH (10 ml) was heated at reflux for 2 h. After
being allowed to cool to room temperature, the aqueous solution was
extracted three times with 15 ml toluene. The organic extract was washed
with 1 N NaOH and water, dried over MgSO4 and evaporated. 36 was
re-crystallized from n-hexane/isopropyl alcohol. Yield: 1.05 g (4.09
mmol), white crystals, 76% M.P.: 111°C TLC (petroleum ether : ethyl
acetate, 2:1): Rf = 0.71 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 9.93 (s, 1H), 8.41 (d,
J = 2.0 Hz, 1H), 7.93 (dd, J = 8.7, 2.1 Hz, 1H), 7.23 (d, J = 7.5 Hz,
2H), 7.05-6.93 (m, 3H), 2.37 (s, 3H) 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ 188.87,
156.56, 151.75, 140.61, 136.26, 134.24, 131.20, 130.50, 127.95, 120.61,
118.67, 21.07 MS (ESI, positive ion mode): [M+H]+ calculated: 258.1,
found: 258.1 CHN analysis: calculated: C: 65.37, H: 4.31, N: 5.44; found:
C: 65.11, H: 4.32, N: 5.55
