$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a 10 mL screw cap pressure tube with a magnetic stir bar were added
CuI (24 mg, 0.125 mmol), 2,2'-bipyridine (39 mg, 0.25 mmol), ethyl
3-hydroxybenzoate (623 mg, 3.75 mmol), 1-bromo-4-chlorobenzene (479 mg,
2.5 mmol), K3PO4 (1.05 g, 5 mmol) and 5 mL DMF. Then the tube was sealed,
placed in an oil bath and stirred at 120 °C for 40 hours. After cooling
to room temperature, the solids were removed by filtration, and the
filter cake washed with 60 mL Et2O. The organic layer was washed with
water (3 × 20 mL), then brine (20 mL) and dried over MgSO4 and
concentrated in vacuo. The residue was purified by chromatography on
silica gel (petroleum ether/AcOEt, 20:1, v/v) to afford S2 (The Br/Cl
selectivity was determined by GC-MS as 166/1).9 Ethyl
3-(4-chlorophenoxy)benzoate (13), Colorless oil, yield 524 mg, 76%. 1H
NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3/TMS): δ 7.73 (d, J= 7.6 Hz, 3H), 7.58 (s, 1H), 7.34
(t, J= 8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.25-7.10 (m, 3H), 6.87 (d, J= 9.2 Hz, 2H), 4.29 (q,
J= 7.3 Hz, 2H), 1.31 (t, J= 7.2 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3/TMS): δ
165.9, 157.0, 155.5, 132.5, 129.91, 129.86, 128.8, 124.7, 123.2, 120.2,
119.7, 61.2, 14.3; IR (film): 3071, 2982, 1721, 1582, 1486, 1443, 1367,
1280, 1235, 1191, 1162, 1098, 1013, 756 cm-1 ; MS (EI, m/z): 276 (M+ ,
100.00), 231 (86.28); HRMS (EI): exact mass calcd for C15H13ClO3 (M+):
276.0553, found: 276.0554.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM sealed tube used
